  <Docs>
    <summary>
            A specialized <see cref="T:Azure.Storage.Files.Shares.ChangeFeed.ShareChangeFeedEvent" /> that represents an Azure Files
            Change Feed reset marker. Reset markers are emitted by the service on events such as
            HardFailover or classic account migration. When observed, log-sequence continuity has
            been broken from this point onward and consumers must decide whether to stop,
            re-baseline, or continue reading past the marker.
            </summary>
    <remarks>
            A reset event is surfaced in-band on <see cref="M:Azure.Storage.Files.Shares.ChangeFeed.ShareChangeFeedClient.GetChanges" />
            enumerations (default <see cref="P:Azure.Storage.Files.Shares.ChangeFeed.ShareChangeFeedResetPolicy.ContinueOnReset" />) at its
            ordered position in the stream, or via <see cref="P:Azure.Storage.Files.Shares.ChangeFeed.ShareChangeFeedResetException.ResetEvent" />
            when the client is configured with <see cref="P:Azure.Storage.Files.Shares.ChangeFeed.ShareChangeFeedResetPolicy.ThrowOnReset" />.
            The base <see cref="P:Azure.Storage.Files.Shares.ChangeFeed.ShareChangeFeedEvent.Reason" /> is always
            <see cref="P:Azure.Storage.Files.Shares.ChangeFeed.ShareChangeFeedReasonKind.Reset" />; the base <see cref="P:Azure.Storage.Files.Shares.ChangeFeed.ShareChangeFeedEvent.Id" />
            holds the reset event GUID as its string form; the base
            <see cref="P:Azure.Storage.Files.Shares.ChangeFeed.ShareChangeFeedEvent.EventOccurredOn" /> holds the reset time.
            </remarks>
  </Docs>
